lique module with a vertices and s<=a outside neighbors can be restored over an induced remainder without increasing the n^2/6+Cn potential when C>=4.","status":"candidate"},{"claim_id":"claim:erdos81-c11-universal-core","text":"A vertex-minimal chordal counterexample to a fixed n^2/6+Cn bound, C>=4, would have fewer than n/2 universal vertices and, with C10, would satisfy 4r<3n+2delta.","status":"candidate"},{"claim_id":"claim:erdos81-c11-imbalance","text":"The interface estimate with error O(a) cannot hold for all a,s: at s=2a its exact excess over (a^2+2as)/6 is 2a^2/3+a/2.","status":"candidate"}],"assumptions":["Finite simple graphs and exact edge partitions.","Doyen-Wilson subsystem existence as proved in the cited Stinson primary paper, with v,w=1 or 3 modulo 6 and v>=2w+1.","C01 complete-split calculation and C10 universal-vertex bound are explicit candidate dependencies.","Allowed axioms: finite-graph-basic, finite-combinatorics, real-arithmetic."],"risks":["No mathematical execution or verifier receipt.","The full design theorem remains an external proof dependency for verification.","Peeling is a conditional induction reduction, not a root proof.","The large-core condition a>=s is essential; arbitrary minority interfaces are not covered."],"open_obligations":["obligation:erdos81-split-extremal-reduction","obligation:erdos81-root"],"failed_route_proposal":null,"source_refs":[{"repository":"vibemathing/problem-erdos-81-chordal-clique-partition","path":"research/records/obligation-graphs.jsonl","revision":"e70735bcaf64d1f1016c3bf4900ea5d8a1d91c4d","relation":"exact"},{"repository":"vibemathing/problem-erdos-81-chordal-clique-partition","path":"research/records/failed-routes.jsonl","revision":"e70735bcaf64d1f1016c3bf4900ea5d8a1d91c4d","relation":"exact"},{"repository":"vibemathing/problem-erdos-81-chordal-clique-partition","path":"research/artifacts/candidates/erdos81-a01-c01-core-obstructions.md","revision":"e70735bcaf64d1f1016c3bf4900ea5d8a1d91c4d","relation